  "body": "## Summary\nThe `TokenWrapper` contract's `transferFrom` function incorrectly emits the `Transfer` event using `msg.sender` (the spender) as the source address instead of the `from` address (the token owner).\n\n## Vulnerability Details\nIn the `transferFrom` function of `src/TokenWrapper.sol`, the code executes the transfer logic correctly (updating allowances and balances) but emits the wrong event data.\n\n```solidity\nfunction transferFrom(address from, address to, uint256 amount) external returns (bool) {\n    // ... allowance checks and balance updates ...\n\n    if (to == address(CORE)) {\n        coreBalance += amount;\n    } else {\n        _balanceOf[to] += amount;\n    }\n    emit Transfer(msg.sender, to, amount); // <--- VULNERABILITY\n    return true;\n}\n```\n\n`msg.sender` in `transferFrom` is the `spender` (the account authorized to move funds), not necessarily the token owner (`from`). The ERC20 standard requires the `Transfer` event to show the movement of tokens from the `from` address to the `to` address.\n\n## Impact\n- **Broken Event Compliance**: The contract violates the ERC20 standard regarding event emission.\n- **Incorrect Indexing**: Off-chain indexers, wallets, and block explorers will incorrectly attribute the source of the transfer. They will show the spender as the sender of funds, rather than the actual token owner.\n- **Protocol Integration Issues**: Other protocols that rely on `Transfer` events to track balances or activity will receive incorrect data.\n\n## Recommended Mitigation\nChange the emitted event to use the `from` parameter:\n\n```diff\n- emit Transfer(msg.sender, to, amount);\n+ emit Transfer(from, to, amount);\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED\npragma solidity >=0.8.30;\n\nimport {Test} from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {TokenWrapper} from \"../src/TokenWrapper.sol\";\nimport {TokenWrapperFactory} from \"../src/TokenWrapperFactory.sol\";\nimport {FullTest} from \"./FullTest.sol\";\nimport {TestToken} from \"./TestToken.sol\";\nimport {IERC20} from \"forge-std/interfaces/IERC20.sol\";\nimport {BaseLocker} from \"../src/base/BaseLocker.sol\";\nimport {ICore} from \"../src/interfaces/ICore.sol\";\nimport {SafeTransferLib} from \"solady/utils/SafeTransferLib.sol\";\nimport {NATIVE_TOKEN_ADDRESS} from \"../src/math/constants.sol\";\nimport {FlashAccountantLib} from \"../src/libraries/FlashAccountantLib.sol\";\n\ncontract TokenWrapperPeriphery is BaseLocker {\n    using FlashAccountantLib for *;\n\n    constructor(ICore core) BaseLocker(core) {}\n\n    function wrap(TokenWrapper wrapper, uint128 amount) external {\n        lock(abi.encode(wrapper, msg.sender, msg.sender, int256(uint256(amount))));\n    }\n    \n    function handleLockData(uint256, bytes memory data) internal override returns (bytes memory) {\n        (TokenWrapper wrapper, address payer, address recipient, int256 amount) =\n            abi.decode(data, (TokenWrapper, address, address, int256));\n\n        if (amount >= 0) {\n            ACCOUNTANT.forward(address(wrapper), abi.encode(amount));\n            if (uint128(uint256(amount)) > 0) {\n                ACCOUNTANT.withdraw(address(wrapper), recipient, uint128(uint256(amount)));\n            }\n            if (uint256(amount) != 0) {\n                if (address(wrapper.UNDERLYING_TOKEN()) == NATIVE_TOKEN_ADDRESS) {\n                    SafeTransferLib.safeTransferETH(address(ACCOUNTANT), uint256(amount));\n                } else {\n                    ACCOUNTANT.payFrom(payer, address(wrapper.UNDERLYING_TOKEN()), uint256(amount));\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        return \"\";\n    }\n}\n\ncontract TokenWrapperPoC is FullTest {\n    TokenWrapperFactory factory;\n    TokenWrapperPeriphery periphery;\n    TestToken underlying;\n    TokenWrapper wrapper;\n\n    event Transfer(address indexed from, address indexed to, uint256 value);\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        FullTest.setUp();\n        underlying = new TestToken(address(this));\n        factory = new TokenWrapperFactory(core);\n        periphery = new TokenWrapperPeriphery(core);\n        \n        wrapper = factory.deployWrapper(IERC20(address(underlying)), 0);\n    }\n\n    function testPoCIncorrectEventEmission() public {\n        address owner = address(0xABCD);\n        address spender = address(0xEF01);\n        address recipient = address(0x1234);\n        uint128 amount = 100 ether;\n\n        // 1. Setup: Owner needs wrapped tokens.\n        // Transfer underlying to owner first\n        underlying.transfer(owner, amount);\n\n        vm.startPrank(owner);\n        // Approve periphery to wrap\n        underlying.approve(address(periphery), amount);\n        // Wrap\n        periphery.wrap(wrapper, amount);\n        \n        // Verify owner has wrapped tokens\n        assertEq(wrapper.balanceOf(owner), amount);\n\n        // Owner approves spender\n        wrapper.approve(spender, amount);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // 2. Spender transfers tokens from Owner to Recipient\n        vm.startPrank(spender);\n        \n        // 3. Expect the INCORRECT event\n        // The bug is that `transferFrom` emits `Transfer(msg.sender, to, amount)`\n        // `msg.sender` is `spender`.\n        // It SHOULD be `from` (owner).\n        \n        vm.expectEmit(true, true, true, true);\n        emit Transfer(spender, recipient, amount); // We expect the BUGGY event: from = spender\n\n        wrapper.transferFrom(owner, recipient, amount);\n        \n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // Verify transfer actually happened correctly in terms of balances\n        assertEq(wrapper.balanceOf(owner), 0);\n        assertEq(wrapper.balanceOf(recipient), amount);\n    }\n}\n```",
